## Evidence

- **The experiment is trustworthy.** The sample ratio matches the documented {{ (1 - r.config.designed_treatment_share) | pct(0) }}/{{ r.config.designed_treatment_share | pct(0) }} split (p = {{ r.srm.p_value | pval }}, **{{ "pass" if r.srm.passed else "FAIL" }}**), and max |SMD| across the 12 features is {{ r.balance_max_abs_smd | num }} (**{{ "pass" if r.balance_max_abs_smd < 0.1 else "FAIL" }}**). Only {{ r.exposure_rate_treated | pct(1) }} of treated users actually saw an ad, so every effect is intent-to-treat: the effect of being *eligible* for ads.
- **Ads work on average.** Visits rise by {{ r.ate.visit.estimate | pp(3) }} (95% CI {{ r.ate.visit.ci_low | pp(3) }} to {{ r.ate.visit.ci_high | pp(3) }}) and conversions by {{ r.ate.conversion.estimate | pp(3) }} (CI {{ r.ate.conversion.ci_low | pp(3) }} to {{ r.ate.conversion.ci_high | pp(3) }}).
- **The model ranks users better than chance on data it never saw.** On a {{ "{:,}".format(r.split_sizes.test) }}-user test split, the {{ r.best_model | replace("_", "-") }} has Qini {{ "%.5f" | format(b.qini_coefficient) }} (CI {{ "%.5f" | format(b.qini_ci[0]) }} to {{ "%.5f" | format(b.qini_ci[1]) }}); the {{ other | replace("_", "-") }} scores {{ "%.5f" | format(r.evaluation[other].qini_coefficient) }}. The depth was chosen on a separate validation split.
- **The uplift is concentrated.** {% set d1 = b.uplift_by_decile[0] %}The top predicted decile shows {{ d1.observed_uplift | pp(2) }} observed uplift against {{ r.ate.visit.estimate | pp(2) }} on average. {% set tail = b.uplift_by_decile[2:] | map(attribute='observed_uplift') | map('abs') | max %}Deciles 3-10 never move more than {{ '%.2f' | format(100 * tail) }} pp from zero, so the model mostly finds one responsive segment.

## When the decision changes

Targeting pays most when ads are expensive. At a {{ cheap.breakeven_uplift | pp(2) }} break-even, the model beats treating everyone by only {{ ((cheap.test_profit_per_user - cheap.test_treat_all_profit_per_user) * 1000) | money }} per 1,000 users, so treating everyone is the simpler policy and gives up little. The appendix tabulates six cost levels.

## Limitations

A seeded {{ "{:,}".format(r.n_rows) }}-row sample ({{ (r.n_rows / 13979592) | pct(1) }} of the file) is used for speed. Uplift is modelled on visits, not conversions. The data is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, so these results are for non-commercial use.
